# Ship after every coding cycle

When a coding cycle finishes (feature, fix, or requested change):

1. Commit relevant project files. Do not wait to be asked.
2. Push `main` to `origin` on GitHub.
3. Netlify builds getlifeos.app from GitHub `main`. Confirm the push landed.
4. Also deploy Railway gateway and platform-admin when API or admin UI changed. Those do not go live from Netlify alone.
5. Never commit secrets (`.env`, tokens, DB URLs, cookie secrets).
